speechtext:
There are 700,000 people in
Montreal. Can you name one individual in Montreal who states that if this road were feasible he would oppose it or name anybody else in the country. No, he cannot, and my hon. friend had to be brought to a round turn by the hon. member for Kings (Mr. Hughes). Personally I am not opposed to the scheme if it is feasible; I should be glad [Mr. Duff.}
to see wheat move from Hudson bay if it were at all possible.
